# f1 = make, f2 = area, f3 = count, f4 = areaOfText, f5 = measure
# `measure` has a guard on `box`, and so a slow body. `area` goes by what its callers leave, and Link proves nothing of `made`: `areaOfText` hands over what only its own test tells.
# What is called here is whatever the second parameter holds: nothing says that the result lies within what the unit has left at `area`. The judge of calls rings.
# RUN: verify-code f2:0:L0 f2:1:i32 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: TypeOutOfDate: f5 SlowBody v5 (CallDirect) hands anything?ResultOfUnknownCallee to entry parameter 0 of f2, which goes by what its callers leave, by what was left there the callee believes L0
# -- code
# code f5:SlowBody {
#   v0: 2 @Int32 = Integer integer=2
#   b0(v1: anything?ParameterOfEscapedFunction @JSValue, v2: anything?ParameterOfEscapedFunction @JSValue) entry=0:
#     v3: Array @Cell = NewArray contents=anything traits=[mayCollect, mayTouchMemory]
#     v4: anything?ResultOfUnknownCallee @JSValue = CallList v2, -, v3 traits=[mayThrow, mayThrowByRule, mayCollect, mayCallUnknownCode, mayBeTerminated, mayWriteWhatIsSeen, mayTouchMemory, mayWriteOutsideObjects]
#     v5: i32 @Int32 = CallDirect v4, v0 function=f2 traits=[mayThrow, mayThrowByRule, mayCollect, mayCallUnknownCode, mayBeTerminated, mayWriteWhatIsSeen, mayTouchMemory, mayWriteOutsideObjects]
